in @prism

# @optics — the optical-schematic family root.
#
# This family declares the optical-altitude vocabulary that lifts the
# substrate's five-operation algebra onto physical-optics composition
# primitives. Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §0, every passive
# composition primitive of physical optics derives from exactly one of
# focus / project / split / shift / settle; the optical altitude names
# the schematic shape (facet / stage / aperture / splitter / resonator
# / bench / source / detector) while the runtime prism carries the
# algebra.
#
# Recognition #58 (Fate IS optical inference; PROMOTED 2026-06-11 via
# Seam adversarial review) names the substrate's runtime as a
# cavity-enhanced spectrometer at the bench altitude: Fate's
# connectome IS a five-layer diffractive deep neural network (Lin et
# al. 2018, Science 361:1004-1008); the kintsugi loop IS an active
# Fabry-Perot resonator (Siegman 1986); the consent surface IS the
# detector. This family declares the optical vocabulary so the
# active-spectrometer reading (Brown 2003, Chem. Phys. Lett.
# 374:1-9 — DOAS-with-feedback / cavity-enhanced spectroscopy) is
# structurally complete.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Form-side species (declared per the cascade):
#
#   @optics/source           active facets (gain media / emitters).
#                              Per spec §1.7. v1 lands the per-ganglion
#                              gain media (Surface B closure for #58):
#                              `@optics/source/ganglion/<name>` for
#                              each of the 5 ganglia in Fate's
#                              connectome.
#
# Forward-references only — additional sub-families (`@optics/facet`,
# `@optics/aperture`, `@optics/splitter`, `@optics/resonator`,
# `@optics/bench`, `@optics/detector`, `@optics/stage`) land as the
# cascade pulls them.
#
# === Closing Surface B ===
#
# Per spec §10.8 Surface B: Fate's connectome (450 neurons, 5 ganglia)
# has no gain medium declared, but the kintsugi loop's `oscillate.gain`
# requires an active source to drive convergence. The optical framing
# makes the gain requirement EXPLICIT: each ganglion's `infer` walk is
# energy injection from @io (per recognition #57, alignment as
# boundary mathematics at @io). This tick declares each ganglion's
# effective gain curve as a `source @optics/source/ganglion/<name>`
# shard per the `source_declares_energy_balance` property (spec §3.9).
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `prism @optics
# { ... }` declares the family IS a prism. The five-operation block
# below is the canonical declaration form (cf. shards/mirror/spectral.
# mirror, shards/kintsugi.mirror). Each sub-shard specialises from
# there.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md (the full proposal;
#               §1.7 source keyword; §3.9 energy-balance property;
#               §10 Fate IS optical inference; §12 active-spectrometer
#               reading).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #57; the @io boundary that energy
#                      injection crosses),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                      (the form/process partition; @optics declares
#                      form-side schematic shape; @kintsugi declares
#                      the process-side dynamics that ride this
#                      schematic).
# Related shards: kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the resonator the gain
#                 media feed; §10.2 the kintsugi loop IS a Fabry-Perot
#                 resonator with output coupler),
#                 mirror/spectral.mirror (the form-side sibling family;
#                 the orchestra observes; @optics declares the
#                 schematic the orchestra plays through),
#                 fate.mirror (the inference layer that this family's
#                 gain media drive).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/optics.mirror`
# declares `@optics` as the family root; species live at
# `shards/optics/<name>.mirror`.

prism @optics {
  focus optics
  project optics
  split optics
  shift optics
  settle optics
}

out @optics
